---
// Static marketing page — no request-time state needed.
// Navigation resolves auth client-side via /api/auth/me (client:load).
export const prerender = true;
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Aspire Sports"
  description="Aspire Sports privacy policy."
>
  <main id="main-content" class="flex-1 pt-24 pb-16 px-4">
    <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto prose prose-ink">
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-display font-bold text-ink mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-ink-muted mb-8">Last updated: April 26, 2026</p>

      <section class="space-y-4 text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          Aspire Sports collects only the information we need to run youth sports programs. This
          page explains what we collect, why, who we share it with, and the choices you have. If
          you have any questions, write to us at
          <a class="text-primary" href="mailto:hello@aspiresportsohio.com">hello@aspiresportsohio.com</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-display font-semibold text-ink mt-8">Information we collect</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
          <li><strong>Parent/guardian:</strong> name, email, phone (optional), hashed password.</li>
          <li><strong>Child participant:</strong> first/last name, birth date, gender (optional), medical notes (optional), emergency contact, and an optional profile photo. We collect this only after you confirm — separately, per child — that you are the parent or legal guardian and consent to its collection.</li>
          <li><strong>Registration &amp; payment history:</strong> programs registered, amounts owed, and payments made. Card details are handled by our payment processor and are not stored on our servers.</li>
          <li><strong>Usage and device data:</strong> pages visited, clicks, approximate region, browser, and timing. Used to keep the site reliable, debug issues, and improve usability.</li>
          <li><strong>Communications:</strong> messages sent through the platform (announcements, coach replies, broadcast notifications).</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-display font-semibold text-ink mt-8">How we use it</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
          <li>Registering and placing children in appropriate programs, teams, and age groups.</li>
          <li>Communicating schedule changes, coach messages, receipts, and reminders.</li>
          <li>Ensuring participant safety, including emergency contact during a session.</li>
          <li>Improving the platform and our programs (in aggregate, not individualized profiling).</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-display font-semibold text-ink mt-8">Children's privacy (COPPA)</h2>
        <p>
          Aspire Sports is intended for parents and guardians, not for children. We collect
          information about children only through their parent's or guardian's account, and only
          after the parent has provided affirmative consent for that specific child. We do not
          knowingly let children under 13 create their own accounts or contact us directly.
        </p>
        <p class="font-semibold text-ink mt-3">As a parent or guardian, you have the right to:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
          <li><strong>Review</strong> what we have collected about your child — visible from your dashboard.</li>
          <li><strong>Correct</strong> any information by editing your child's record from the dashboard.</li>
          <li><strong>Delete</strong> your child's record at any time using the "Delete record" button on the family-members card. Deletion removes their profile, photos, registrations (where unpaid), team rosters, and assessment history. If your child has paid registrations on file, contact us — we will process the refund and complete the deletion.</li>
          <li><strong>Refuse</strong> further collection or use by deleting the record and closing your account.</li>
          <li><strong>Withdraw photo consent</strong> by removing the photo from your child's profile, which clears the consent record.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">
          For COPPA-related questions or to make any of the requests above:
          <a class="text-primary" href="mailto:hello@aspiresportsohio.com">hello@aspiresportsohio.com</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-display font-semibold text-ink mt-8">Third-party services</h2>
        <p>
          We do not sell personal information. We share information only with vendors needed to
          deliver the service, and only the minimum required:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
          <li><strong>Stripe</strong> — payment processing. Card data flows directly from your browser to Stripe; we never see or store it.</li>
          <li><strong>Resend</strong> — transactional email (receipts, schedule updates, password resets) sent to parent/guardian addresses only.</li>
          <li><strong>Cloudinary</strong> — secure hosting for profile photos.</li>
          <li><strong>Telegram</strong> — optional channel for coach-to-parent team messaging. Only parents/guardians who opt in see these messages.</li>
          <li><strong>PostHog</strong> — product analytics, error tracking, and session replay (described below).</li>
          <li><strong>Netlify &amp; Railway</strong> — application hosting and database hosting.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-display font-semibold text-ink mt-8">Analytics &amp; session replay</h2>
        <p>
          We use PostHog to record anonymous usage events (page views, clicks, scroll depth) and
          to capture session replays so we can debug usability problems. <strong>All text and
          form inputs are masked by default in replays</strong>, so children's names, dates of
          birth, photos, medical notes, and contact details are not captured in the recording —
          only the layout, mouse motion, and click targets. We do not use this data for ad
          targeting or sell it to third parties. If you would prefer to opt out of analytics
          entirely, contact us and we will exclude your account.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-display font-semibold text-ink mt-8">Your choices</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
          <li>Update your profile or family members from your dashboard.</li>
          <li>Opt out of marketing email at any time — operational messages (schedule, safety, receipts) continue while you have an active registration.</li>
          <li>Request deletion of your data; we retain payment records for the period required by tax and accounting law (typically 7 years), with personal identifiers removed where possible.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-display font-semibold text-ink mt-8">Security</h2>
        <p>
          We use industry-standard encryption in transit and at rest, and we limit internal access
          to a need-to-know basis. No system is perfectly secure; if we discover a material
          incident affecting your data, we will notify you.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-display font-semibold text-ink mt-8">Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Privacy questions or requests:
          <a class="text-primary" href="mailto:hello@aspiresportsohio.com">hello@aspiresportsohio.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
